sara: heads up - PR #848 is a bulk migration to the new tool-calling + structured-output patterns. blocking items before i merge: updated SDK examples (py + ts), clearer JSON schema examples for optional arrays and enums, a short "fallback" pattern for when parsing fails, and two broken links i hit in the guide. who can take which?

alex: i can do SDK examples. i'll convert the old `call_function()` snippets to `client.invoke_tool()` and add a tiny streaming example (chunked tool output -> yield to client). keeping examples minimal.

toni: i'll tackle the schema examples. leaning toward `oneOf` for optional objects/arrays and a small section on canonicalization (normalize null/empty -> []). will add a JS canonicalize helper.

rahul: i'll write the ops-facing fallback + metric guidance: what to log, metric names (docs suggestion: `parse.fail`, `parse.fallback_used`), and sample envelope for unparseable payloads. also recommend a 3-attempt retry with small jitter before fallback.

docs-ci-bot: quick check triggered: docs/lint -> running link-audit and snippet-runner. results in ~3m.

sara: broken links i found: `/docs/guides/structured-output` (should be `/docs/guides/structured-output-handbook`) and an outdated anchor `/reference#function_calling` -> `/reference#tool-calling`. left inline comments in the PR.

alex: noted. i'll patch the anchors when i push snippets. pushing in ~30m.

toni: here's the canonicalization snippet i'll add (JS, slightly different form):
```js
// normalize.js
function normalizeList(input) {
  if (Array.isArray(input)) return input;
  if (input === null || input === undefined) return [];
  try {
    const parsed = typeof input === 'string' ? JSON.parse(input) : input;
    return Array.isArray(parsed) ? parsed : [parsed];
  } catch (e) {
    return [String(input)];
  }
}
```

rahul: sample fallback policy pseudocode i'll add to docs:
```py
# fallback_policy.py
for attempt in range(3):
  parsed = try_parse(json_text)
  if parsed and validate(parsed, schema):
    emit_metric('parse.success')
    return parsed
  sleep(backoff(attempt))
emit_metric('parse.fail')
emit_metric('parse.fallback_used')
return {"error": "unparseable", "hint": "see docs/guides/structured-output-handbook#fallbacks"}
```

alex: small note on SDK snippet style: show sync + async streaming variants. TS example will use `await client.invokeTool({name, input})` and a streaming one using `.stream()` iterator. keeping to 6-8 lines each.

toni: also adding a short paragraph recommending `oneOf` for nullable objects: example will show `oneOf: [{type: 'object', properties: {...}}, {type: 'null'}]` instead of `type: ['object','null']` and explain parser compatibility.

docs-ci-bot: link-audit finished - 2 broken links (see comments). snippet-runner found one snippet runtime warning (stream example missing await).

sara: ok owners: alex -> SDK snippets + fix stream await in snippet, toni -> schema examples + canonicalization helper, rahul -> fallback + metrics + ops envelope. i'll do a final pass and re-run CI. aim to merge by tomorrow morning.

